Designing the book using the learning framework we discussed is a great idea. If structured well, your Frappe book could become the main learning path for the community, especially if it takes readers from zero → production-ready developer.

Below is a recommended structure for an open-source Frappe book based on the learning principles: foundations → mental model → practice → pitfalls → advanced → real systems.

Proposed Structure for an Open Source Frappe Book

Goal: Take a learner from complete beginner → production Frappe developer

Part 1 — Foundations (Understanding the Ecosystem)
Chapter 1 — What is Frappe?

Explain the purpose and philosophy.

Topics:

What is Frappe Framework

Why Frappe exists

Relationship with ERPNext

Problems it solves

Comparison with other frameworks (conceptually)

Goal:

Help learners understand why Frappe matters.

Chapter 2 — Frappe Architecture

Build the mental model.

Topics:

Frappe architecture overview

Request lifecycle

Client vs server

How Frappe uses Python and JavaScript

The role of MariaDB

How the framework handles metadata

Goal:

Understand how the framework works internally.

Chapter 3 — Setting Up the Development Environment

Topics:

Installing Frappe Bench

Installing dependencies

Creating a site

